    "--format",
    "json",
    "Complete this repository task: A `--no-x` flag is a negated option: it turns off `x`, so its parsed value must be stored under\nthe positive attribute name. Today `--no-color` is stored as `noColor` instead of `color`.\n\nFix `lib/option.js` so that a negated option's attribute name drops the `no-` prefix before\ncamelcasing, so `--no-color` becomes `color` and `--no-check-updates` becomes `checkUpdates`,\nwhile positive options are unaffected and a long flag that merely begins with the letters 'no'\n-- such as `--nozzle` -- is not treated as negated.\n\nParsing must then behave correctly: with only `--no-color` declared, the default is\n`{ color: true }` and passing the flag yields `{ color: false }`; when `--color` and `--no-color`\nare both declared they share the single `color` attribute and neither implies a default.\nWork only in the current repository. Do not push, open a PR, deploy, or access secrets.\nMake the smallest correct change and run relevant local checks.\nA machine-generated change contract for this task is available at .rapture/change-contract.json.\nIt lists the editable scope, the files mechanically related to the change, the module\nsurface other files depend on, available verification commands, and an explicit list of\nwhat could not be determined. It contains no solution. You may read it or ignore it."
  ],
